        "A student from the Maharashtra board arrives with a strong algebra and calculus toolkit and little practice at justifying a result. Analysis and Approaches builds on that toolkit and adds proof, functions as transformations and, at Higher Level, a Paper 3 that sets one extended problem-solving task. The Mathematical Exploration, an independent piece of writing worth a fifth of the grade, is usually the first thing a state-board student has never done.",
        "Applications and Interpretation leans the other way: modelling with real data, statistics and the graphic display calculator, which suits students heading for economics, business, psychology or design. It is often mistaken for the easier Maths. At Higher Level it is not, and a student who picks it for that reason is surprised by the volume of technology work.",
